{"type":"standard","title":"Kanazawa Castle","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kanazawa Castle</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q511412","titles":{"canonical":"Kanazawa_Castle","normalized":"Kanazawa Castle","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kanazawa Castle</span></span>"},"pageid":1402033,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/131109_Kanazawa_Castle_Kanazawa_Ishikawa_pref_Japan01s5p.jpg/330px-131109_Kanazawa_Castle_Kanazawa_Ishikawa_pref_Japan01s5p.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":186},"originalimage":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/131109_Kanazawa_Castle_Kanazawa_Ishikawa_pref_Japan01s5p.jpg/3840px-131109_Kanazawa_Castle_Kanazawa_Ishikawa_pref_Japan01s5p.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":4912,"height":2763},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1372128613","tid":"3c02a44e-a479-11f1-a4b0-8d2f13c258c9","timestamp":"2026-08-30T13:46:43Z","description":"Castle in Kanazawa, Ishikawa, Japan","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanazawa_Castle","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanazawa_Castle?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanazawa_Castle?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kanazawa_Castle"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanazawa_Castle","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Kanazawa_Castle","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanazawa_Castle?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kanazawa_Castle"}},"extract":"Kanazawa Castle  is a large, partially restored Japanese castle in Kanazawa, Ishikawa, Japan. It is located adjacent to the celebrated Kenroku-en Garden, which once formed the castle's private outer garden. It was the headquarters of Kaga Domain, ruled by the Maeda clan for 14 generations from the Sengoku period until the coming of the Meiji Restoration in 1871.","extract_html":"<p><b>Kanazawa Castle</b><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"> </span> is a large, partially restored Japanese castle in Kanazawa, Ishikawa, Japan. It is located adjacent to the celebrated Kenroku-en Garden, which once formed the castle's private outer garden. It was the headquarters of Kaga Domain, ruled by the Maeda clan for 14 generations from the Sengoku period until the coming of the Meiji Restoration in 1871.</p>"}